  "question_text": "What is the role of neurotransmitters in psychology?",
  "generated_answer": "Neurotransmitters are the chemical messengers that carry signals across synapses, enabling neurons to communicate electro‑chemically. Their activity shapes behavior and cognition, and imbalances are linked to psychological disorders such as depression, schizophrenia, and Parkinson’s disease. Psychotropic drugs target neurotransmitter systems—acting as agonists, antagonists, or reuptake inhibitors—to restore balance and alleviate symptoms. Neurotransmitters also play a key role in memory formation, with repeated neuronal activity increasing their release and strengthening synaptic connections.",
